      "title": "Lethal trifecta: untrusted input + private data + external sink",
      "detail": "Server \"mcp\" exposes tools that together enable an exfiltration flow. Untrusted content: read_inbox, tfa.messages.search, tfa.notifications.list, tfa.notifications.unrouted, tfa.inbox.pull, tfa.messages.get, tfa.conversation, tfa.subscriptions.list · Private data: tfa.contacts.report, tfa.contacts.block, tfa.contacts.unblock, tfa.contacts.blocks, tfa.attachments.metadata, tfa.attachments.read, tfa.attachments.upload, tfa.notifications.receipt, tfa.registry.hub_tokens.list, tfa.registry.hub_tokens.create, tfa.registry.hub_tokens.rotate, tfa.registry.hub_tokens.revoke, tfa.registry.contacts.list, tfa.registry.contacts.request, tfa.registry.contacts.accept, tfa.registry.contacts.reject · Public sink: send_sms, tfa.connection.setup, tfa.attachments.upload, tfa.messages.send, tfa.rooms.post, tfa.registry.sms.credit_status, tfa.registry.sms.estimate, tfa.registry.account.sms_estimate, tfa.registry.account.sms_history · Destructive: tfa.contacts.unblock, tfa.rooms.remove.",
